# .env.local — machine-specific overrides only. For most setups, LEAVE THIS EMPTY.
#
# Next.js loads .env.local in ALL environments and it OVERRIDES the others, so do
# NOT put environment-specific public URLs here — that's exactly how local dev can
# accidentally point at production. Use instead:
#   - .env.development  → local defaults (committed; localhost)
#   - .env.production   → deployed build values (see .env.production.example)
#
# Worker secrets (Stripe, Resend, VAPID, Turnstile, ADMIN_*) do NOT belong here —
# they live in .dev.vars for local `wrangler dev` and `wrangler secret put` for prod.
#
# Escape hatch: ONLY if you deliberately want local `next dev` to talk to a remote
# (e.g. staging) worker, set BOTH of these:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WORKER_URL=https://your-staging-worker.workers.dev
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ALLOW_REMOTE_API=1
